※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ What a `foreach` takes out of what it walks points where the whole did: an element of a
※ list made in an arena is in the arena.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let s: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(s)
    let l: [str] = [("a" ⧺ "b" in s), ("c" ⧺ "d" in s)] in s
    let n: mut u8 = 0u8
    foreach one: str = l:
        ⎕empty(s)
        if one = "ab":
            n ← n + 1u8
    if n = 1u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
